<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's short-term PHIBOR rates higher.</title>
<headline>Manila's short-term PHIBOR rates higher.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were higher at the short end of the curve from one to two weeks, while the rest were either steady or lower, traders said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A trader said the short-term rates rose in step with the rise in money market rates.</p>
<p>&quot;But the longer ones were almost the same because the long-term view is that interest rates will go down,&quot; the same dealer said.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  NOV 19		 NOV 18</p>
<p>    1 W		11 15/16		11 11/16</p>
<p>    2 W		11 13/16		11  5/8</p>
<p>    1 M		11  9/16		11  9/16</p>
<p>    2 M		11  1/2		 11  1/2</p>
<p>    3 M		11  9/16		11  5/8</p>
<p>    6 M		11  3/4		 11 13/16</p>
<p>    12M		11  7/8		 11  7/8</p>
<p>    VAL		20-Nov		  19-Nov</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
